# RBAC & Authorization

## Permission Format

`{module}.{resource}.{action}` — register in `PermissionCatalog.cs`

Examples:
- `students.profile.create`
- `attendance.records.mark`
- `fees.payments.collect`
- `roles.permissions.assign`

## Command/Query Authorization

```csharp
[RequirePermission("students.profile.create")]
public record CreateStudentCommand(...) : IRequest<Result<Guid>>;
```

`AuthorizationBehavior` reads attribute before handler executes.

## Scope-Based Access

- Teachers: scoped to assigned class(es) via `IScopeResolver`
- Accountants: tenant-wide for fees, no student PII beyond billing
- Parents: `Self` scope — only linked children
- Apply scope in **query handlers**, not just UI hiding

## Role Rules

- System roles (`IsSystem = true`) cannot be deleted or renamed
- Permission changes invalidate Redis cache: `permissions:{userId}`

## Frontend/Mobile Mirror

- Angular: `*hasPermission="'students.profile.create'"` + `PermissionGuard`
- Never rely on UI-only hiding — API must enforce
